From 82d228fa7ea08e234b7e7cbcedf1faef54a1a2d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lsyyyyyyy <lsyyyyyyy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 22:14:43 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] partition: recognize the mifs filesystem type

Xiaomi HyperOS 2+ devices ship /data formatted with "mifs", which is
their f2fs fork (driver registers the fs as "mifs"). Without it TWRP
logs "Unknown File System: mifs" and refuses to mount /data.

Verified on a Redmi K60 Ultra (corot, Android 16, HyperOS 3).
---
 partition.cpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/partition.cpp b/partition.cpp
index 8c53567..08a535d 100755
--- a/partition.cpp
+++ b/partition.cpp
@@ -1189,6 +1189,7 @@ bool TWPartition::Is_File_System(string File_System) {
 		File_System == "yaffs2" ||
 		File_System == "exfat" ||
 		File_System == "f2fs" ||
+		File_System == "mifs" ||
 		File_System == "erofs" ||
 		File_System == "squashfs" ||
 		File_System == "auto")
